! A square sheet of hydrogen in vacuum: the cheapest cell that is a
! two-dimensional material with a tip plane above it and a substrate plane
! below. Used by tests/regression/test_transport.py (PLAN.md P66), whose
! checks are identities rather than comparisons with another code -- no code
! computes this quantity, so what validates it is the Tersoff-Hamann limit
! against run_stm, the spin partition, and the agreement of the three spin
! regimes.
!
! nosym and one k-division along the stacking axis are both required by the
! quantity: lateral momentum is conserved exactly and the momentum along the
! normal is not, and a symmetry-reduced wedge symmetrises the map over
! operations that exchange the tip side with the substrate side.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 6, celldm(1) = 5.0, celldm(3) = 3.0,
    nat = 1, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 15.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.05
    nosym = .true.
    nbnd = 8
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 H  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 H 0.0 0.0 0.5
K_POINTS {automatic}
 4 4 1 0 0 0
